# L §5.15: crps(normal(m, s), y) to u is correctly rounded (not a rational on a cell edge: printed with ≈ and
# the bound u/2 = 0.0000000005, L §7.3).  Its digits are not asserted (a transcendental value).
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01

input y: num
def c: num = crps(normal(0, 1), y) to 1e-9 at reader

version v
  cite s
  governs 2026..
  known 2026-01-01
  y = 0

ask a: c law 2026-06-30 orient lower
=== expect
a: ≈ 0.2 ...
  law date 2026-06-30, cut 2026-12-31
  orient lower
